  // Word's own multi-level numbering, so inserting or deleting a clause
  // renumbers everything after it. Level 0 "1.", level 1 "1.1", level 2
  // "(a)" — and front matter and the execution block stay out of it.
  //
  // The list APIs are the most host-dependent surface this tool touches, so
  // when any part of this refuses, the literal labels _diLayout already
  // computed are written into the text instead. A statically numbered
  // contract is a far better outcome than an unnumbered one.
